    <p class="tag">Specialised Service</p>
    <h1>Lost Your Passport in the Philippines?</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Practical guidance for a stressful situation.</p>

    <p>We can help you understand the immigration steps that may follow the loss or replacement of your passport, and coordinate the relevant immigration documentation once a replacement travel document has been issued by the appropriate embassy or consular authority.</p>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Explaining the immigration steps that typically follow a lost or replaced passport</li>
      <li>Coordinating the relevant immigration documentation once your replacement travel document is issued</li>
      <li>Liaising with the Bureau of Immigration on your behalf, where representation is permitted</li>
      <li>Helping you avoid unnecessary delays to your onward travel or stay</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What to Expect</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Contact your embassy or consulate</h3>
        <p>Passport issuance and replacement is handled solely by your country's embassy or consulate in the Philippines.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Reach out to us</h3>
        <p>Once you have, or are in the process of obtaining, a replacement travel document, tell us about your situation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Immigration coordination</h3>
        <p>We coordinate the related Philippine immigration processing and record updates on your behalf.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="context-note">
      <p>Foreign Immigration Services does not issue passports. Our role concerns the related Philippine immigration processing and record updates once your replacement travel document has been issued.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="service-cta">
      <h2>Lost Your Passport?</h2>
      <p>Tell us your situation and we will explain the steps that apply to you.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=lost-passport">Get Travel Document Assistance</a></p>
